  "observed": [
    "Cancel/reconcile carry a distinct saved decision ID and original target ID. Reusing the target ID is refused before submission.",
    "Completed message, conversation-creation and Session-end cancellation receipts report already_terminal and preserve the completed target; they do not claim rollback.",
    "Decision references preserve known original cid/sid assertions, omit target connid and restore/query the original decision on a fresh client. Empty original assertions remain empty.",
    "Replaying the same decision is stable. Changing its target under the same ID, deciding a prior decision, forged evidence and an incompatible requested terminal outcome are refused by the production host.",
    "Nonempty decision extensions refuse before I/O because the installed action model does not persist them in intent identity.",
    "Controlled signed receipts prove a completed decision may still report an unknown target, and reconciliation decoding preserves attributed evidence. Mismatched target data and server503 preserve original decision uncertainty. Positive reconciliation here is protocol-only, not backend evidence qualification.",
    "Receipt target is OperationId, because wire data does not disclose the original target command/scope. All language declarations and the source checker enforce that boundary.",
    "Existing message/Participant/Session cases remain passing."
  ],
